---
/**
 * Booking-engine handoff tracking.
 *
 * Fires one `booking_handoff` dataLayer event per click on any vendor
 * "Book now" control, so the closest thing we have to revenue stops being
 * counted nowhere. Counts ATTEMPTS, never bookings: both checkouts open in
 * vendor-hosted overlays we cannot see into, and neither navigates away
 * (12 months of GA4: 1 `wetravel*` session, 0 `fareharbor*`), so completions
 * exist only in WeTravel's and FareHarbor's own dashboards.
 *
 * Two vendors, two completely different shapes:
 *  - WeTravel  — a `<button class="wtrvl-checkout_button" data-uuid="…">`
 *                carrying `href` as a plain ATTRIBUTE (vendor quirk).
 *  - FareHarbor — a real `<a href="…/embeds/book/…/items/<id>/…">`.
 *
 * WHY `dataLayer.push({ event })` AND NOT `gtag('event', …)` — measured on the
 * live site 15 Oct 2026 over CDP, because the two look equivalent and are not:
 *
 *  1. GA4 (G-RXEF72Y3WV) is loaded BY the GTM container (gtag/js arrives with
 *     `cx=c`), so GTM owns `window.dataLayer`. A gtag-form push
 *     (`dataLayer.push(arguments)`) is left untouched in the array — no
 *     `gtm.uniqueEventId` stamped, no `/g/collect` request. Dead on arrival.
 *     The same push on a standalone gtag.js page DOES hit `/g/collect`, which
 *     is why the gtag advice is true in general and false here.
 *  2. This form IS ingested: GTM stamped `gtm.uniqueEventId` on it and the
 *     container's data model then read back `event` and `vendor`.
 *  3. Do not route this through the `gtag()` helper in CookieConsent.astro.
 *     It is doubly unreachable: Astro wraps `define:vars` inline scripts in an
 *     IIFE so the function is never global (`window.gtag` is `undefined` live),
 *     and it pushes a rest ARRAY (`dataLayer.push(args)`) where gtag requires
 *     an `arguments` object — the array form produced zero hits even on a clean
 *     gtag.js page.
 *
 * So this half is the half that lives in the repo. Forwarding it to GA4 needs
 * one Custom Event trigger (`booking_handoff`) plus one GA4 Event tag in
 * GTM-KRC3B4ZQ; until that exists the event is visible in GTM Preview and
 * nowhere else. See TOP-60.
 *
 * NOT consent-gated, on purpose. The container grants `analytics_storage`
 * unconditionally for all regions and its consent `update` only ever touches
 * the `ad_*` keys, so analytics is never blocked here — and a `cc_cookie`
 * gate is precisely what made `form_submission` useless.
 */
---

<script is:inline>
  (function () {
    // One delegated listener per page. The listener lives on `document`, which
    // survives Astro's view-transition body swaps, but this inline script is
    // re-executed on every swap — hence the guard. Without it, a visitor six
    // pages deep would fire six events per click.
    if (window.__bookingHandoffBound) return;
    window.__bookingHandoffBound = true;

    const WETRAVEL_SELECTOR = '.wtrvl-checkout_button';
    const FAREHARBOR_SELECTOR = 'a[href*="fareharbor.com/embeds/book"]';

    document.addEventListener(
      'click',
      function (event) {
        const target = event.target;
        // Guard rather than assume: a click inside an <svg> icon targets an
        // SVGElement, and text nodes have no `closest`.
        if (!target || typeof target.closest !== 'function') return;

        // `.closest()` is required, not cosmetic — the raw click target is
        // normally the label text or an inner <span>, so reading dataset off
        // `event.target` returns undefined.
        const wetravel = target.closest(WETRAVEL_SELECTOR);
        const fareharbor = wetravel
          ? null
          : target.closest(FAREHARBOR_SELECTOR);
        const element = wetravel || fareharbor;
        if (!element) return;

        let packageId = '(unknown)';
        if (wetravel) {
          // WeTravel's `data-uuid` is the package, which is the whole point:
          // it separates "someone clicked" from "someone wanted the guided
          // trip rather than the self-guided one".
          packageId = wetravel.getAttribute('data-uuid') || '(unknown)';
        } else {
          const match = (fareharbor.getAttribute('href') || '').match(
            /items\/(\d+)/
          );
          if (match) packageId = match[1];
        }

        window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
        window.dataLayer.push({
          event: 'booking_handoff',
          vendor: wetravel ? 'wetravel' : 'fareharbor',
          package_id: packageId,
          tour_path: location.pathname,
          // GA4 caps parameter values at 100 chars; 40 is plenty for a CTA and
          // keeps the cardinality low enough to be readable in a report.
          cta_label: (element.textContent || '').trim().slice(0, 40)
        });
      },
      // Capture phase. Both vendors bind their own click handlers to these
      // elements to open the checkout overlay; if either ever calls
      // stopPropagation() a bubble-phase listener on document would never run
      // and we would lose every click silently.
      true
    );
  })();
</script>
